<article class="env-lemma" id="0F1P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F1P">Lemma <span data-tag="0F1P">59.97.9</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a separably closed field. Let $X$ and $Y$ be finite type schemes over $k$. Let $n \geq 1$ be an integer invertible in $k$. Then for $E \in D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z})$ and $K \in D(Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z})$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\Gamma (X \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)} Y, \text{pr}_1^{-1}E \otimes _{\mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z}}^\mathbf {L} \text{pr}_2^{-1}K ) = R\Gamma (X, E) \otimes _{\mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z}}^\mathbf {L} R\Gamma (Y, K)  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0F1N" data-tag="0F1N">59.97.8</a> we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  R\text{pr}_{1, *}( \text{pr}_1^{-1}E \otimes _{\mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z}}^\mathbf {L} \text{pr}_2^{-1}K) = E \otimes _{\mathbf{Z}/n\mathbf{Z}}^\mathbf {L} \underline{R\Gamma (Y, K)}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       We conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F12" data-tag="0F12">59.96.5</a> which we may use because $\text{cd}(X) < \infty $ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F10" data-tag="0F10">59.96.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>